      "message": "\u003e what tooling is flagging this as an issue\n\nMy very own rationality-limited eyes are flagging the issue 😊\n\nI understand that net does not import ssh; I am aware that my patch is not addressing any security issue, but rather I am proposing a quality-of-life improvement.\n\nLet\u0027s say I am a package owner, and I find this line in my go.sum:\ngolang.org/x/crypto v0.0.0-20190308221718-c2843e01d9a2/go.mod h1:djNgcEr1/C05ACkg1iLfiJU5Ep61QUkGW8qpdssI0+w\u003d\n\nKnowing that CVE-2020-29652 was fixed in v0.0.0-20201203163018-be400aefbc4c, how can I be sure I am not really depending on the vulnerable logic of the vulnerable lib? I thought that just removing that line (by explicitly bumping the dependency) was the best way of clearing out the concern. But apparently there\u0027s a better way?",
